# Conventional Commits

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

**Description:** imperative, lowercase, max 50 characters, no trailing period.

## Types

`feat` `fix` `docs` `style` `refactor` `perf` `test` `build` `ci` `chore` `revert`

Breaking: `feat!:` / `fix!:` or footer `BREAKING CHANGE: …`.

During modernization, **product** version digits come from `.cursor/skills/version-bump/SKILL.md` (usually 3rd digit). Do not treat `feat` as SemVer MINOR for `app/system/config.php`.

## Examples

```
feat(system): add widget management UI
fix(blog): prevent XSS in comments
docs: update installation guide
refactor(orm): modernize query builder API
ci(conductor): cap PLAN job repeats
chore(deps): update doctrine/dbal to 3.x
```

PR labels from commit type: `.cursor/rules/github-labels.mdc`. Changelog text is written by the doc-writer / push skill — commits are not auto-parsed into `CHANGELOG-NEW.md`.

## Pull requests

PR titles use the same subject line. Pass `--title` to `gh pr create`; do not copy a GitHub
issue title (`Step X.Y: Name` is for issues only). When the PR closes a ROADMAP step, append
` (Step X.Y)` after the subject — the suffix is extra and does not count against the
50-character description:

```
feat(extension): extension safety and fault isolation (Step 2.7)
feat(installer): add snapshot three-stage uninstall (Step 2.7.1)
```

Tooling with no ROADMAP row: conventional title only, no Step suffix. Full title rules:
`.cursor/skills/push/SKILL.md`.
